Valid

Validity can be compromised if a student does not
understand what is being asked of them. For example,
one valid method of assessing a student’s knowledge
and understanding is to question them. If the questions
posed are difficult for the student to understand (not
in terms of the content but the way they are phrased,
for example) the validity of the assessment method is
questionable.

