+    "lesson": 6,
+    "field": "flashcard_questions",
+    "path": "[8].a",
+    "expect": "Employers must provide safe working conditions including ergonomic equipment and screen break guidelines.",
+    "value": "Employers must protect workers’ health and safety so far as is reasonably practicable.",
+    "severity": "HIGH",
+    "note": "F6: Removes the incorrect attribution of screen-break rules."
+  },
+  {
+    "lesson": 8,
+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "The <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"The global system of interconnected computer networks that uses internet protocols to connect devices worldwide, distinct from the World Wide Web, which is the collection of websites and resources accessed via the internet.\">internet</dfn> and the <strong>World Wide Web (WWW)</strong> are the infrastructure that makes IoE possible. The internet provides the underlying network connections; the WWW provides the web-based interfaces through which people access and interact with IoE systems. Without both, devices could not communicate across locations or be controlled remotely.",
+    "replace": "The <dfn class=\"term\" data-def=\"The global system of interconnected computer networks that uses internet protocols to connect devices worldwide, distinct from the World Wide Web, which is the collection of websites and resources accessed via the internet.\">internet</dfn> provides network connections for IoE devices. The <strong>World Wide Web (WWW)</strong> can provide web-based interfaces through which people access and control IoE systems, but devices can also communicate using other internet protocols.",
+    "severity": "MEDIUM",
+    "note": "F7: The web is not required for IoE device communication."
