+    "note": "F10: ChromeOS also supports installed Android and Linux applications."
+  },
+  {
+    "lesson": 10,
+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": " is Google&rsquo;s lightweight operating system found on Chromebook devices, popular in schools. Its HCI is almost entirely browser-based: apps run in Chrome tabs rather than as locally installed programs. This has significant design implications &mdash; Chrome OS users expect web applications, and offline functionality is limited. Designers building for Chrome OS must prioritise responsive web design and cloud-based workflows.",
+    "replace": " is Google&rsquo;s operating system for Chromebook devices, popular in schools. It supports web apps and, on compatible devices, Android and Linux applications. Designers should consider responsive web design, native-app patterns and offline use.",
+    "severity": "MEDIUM",
+    "note": "F10: Removes the false browser-only description."
+  },
+  {
+    "lesson": 10,
+    "field": "practice_questions",
+    "path": "[0].text",
+    "expect": "Which operating system runs on Chromebook laptops and delivers most of its functionality through a browser rather than locally installed applications?",
