+      "lesson": 6,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "The Computer Misuse Act creates three criminal offences ... modifying computer data without authorisation.",
+      "truth": "The current Act covers unauthorised access and unauthorised acts intended to impair computer operation; its modern section 3 is not simply an offence of unauthorised data modification.",
+      "evidence": "Police and Justice Act 2006 explanatory notes, section 36; Serious Crime Act 2015 explanatory notes",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F6",
+      "lesson": 6,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "The Health and Safety at Work Act ... includes ... offering regular breaks from screen use.",
+      "truth": "The Health and Safety at Work Act imposes a general safety duty. Breaks for display-screen users are specifically governed by the Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992.",
+      "evidence": "HSE: Should VDU users be given breaks?; HSE: Health and Safety at Work Act 1974",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F7",
+      "lesson": 8,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "Without both, devices could not communicate across locations or be controlled remotely.",
+      "truth": "The internet provides the network. The World Wide Web is an information system on the internet and can provide an IoE interface, but IoE devices can communicate through other internet protocols.",
+      "evidence": "W3C: What is the difference between the web and the internet?; IETF IoT interoperability material",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F8",
+      "lesson": 8,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "The seven application areas are: energy management, health, manufacturing, military/emergency services, smart devices (business/home/personal) and transport.",
+      "truth": "R050 lists six top-level IoE application areas: energy management, health, manufacturing, military/emergency services, smart devices and transport. Business, home and personal are subcategories of smart devices.",
+      "evidence": "spec 4.2 Topic Area 6.2",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
