+      "claim": "The specification names Chrome OS among the eight operating systems.",
+      "truth": "The specification literally says ‘Chrome’, while Google’s operating-system name is ChromeOS. Recommendation: retain the product name but make a future curriculum-wide wording decision such as ‘ChromeOS (called Chrome in the specification)’.",
+      "evidence": "spec 4.2 Topic Area 2.3; Google Chromebook Help",
+      "verdict": "ADJUDICATE"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F15",
+      "lesson": 11,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "A one-word answer such as ‘email’ without justification scores zero on a 3-mark question.",
+      "truth": "The specification does not prescribe a 3-mark device-recommendation question or a per-point mark allocation. Recommendation: retain general advice to justify choices, but do not state a guaranteed zero without the specific question and mark scheme.",
+      "evidence": "spec 4.2 Assessment guidance and 5.1 Overview of the assessment",
